# Engineering

## Lifecycle (one ticket per chat, one skill per chat)
- Tickets: `docs/tasks/<ID>-<slug>.md`; index: `docs/tasks/README.md`.
  Status: todo → in progress → in review → done. Only lifecycle skills change status.
- `/refine`: sync, pick ticket, grill (max 8), write Decisions + Files + Verify. No code.
- `/implement`: build from ticket only, code-review, Outcome, `gt create` + `gt submit`.
- `/address`: fix PR comments on the same branch, `gt modify` + `gt submit`.
- `/done`: after human merges, sync, mark done, name next ticket.
- Ticket work without a skill: name the skill that fits and stop.
- Bugs: new chat + `/diagnosing-bugs` (`.agents/skills`).

## Git
- Allowed: `gt sync -f`, `gt checkout`, `gt create -am "<type(scope): subject>"`, `gt submit`, `gt modify -a`, read-only `gh`.
- Exception: `/refine` and `/done` may commit only `docs/tasks/**` on main:
  `git commit -m "chore(tasks): …"` and `git push origin main`.
- Forbidden: other commits on main, `git reset`, `git rebase`, `git push --force`, `gt merge`.
  Human merges feature PRs on GitHub.
- Never edit files listed in another `in progress` or `in review` ticket.
- Never bundle a refactor with a feature. Never add a dependency without one sentence of why.

## Quality gates
- No agent-run headless Godot (token-heavy). Put a ≤5-bullet `## Verify` checklist for the human.
- If a quiet `just test-q` (PASS/FAIL only) exists later, prefer it; until then skip automated Godot in skills.
- Before `gt create`: run `code-review` (`.agents/skills`) with fixed point = ticket `base`, spec = ticket file. Fix real findings.
- Call `tdd` only when Decisions name a seam **and** a quiet test recipe exists.
- Logical file budget: paired `.gd` + `.tscn` counts as **one**. More than ~5 → split into stacked tickets before building.
- Unsure between two designs: two lines each, ask. Never build both.

## Token discipline
- Context between chats = the ticket file only (Goal, Decisions, Files, Verify). No temp handoffs for routine tickets.
- Start from the ticket and its Files. Codebase search for gaps; open extra files one at a time.
- Never bulk-read the repo, `.godot/`, `build/`, `audio/` binaries, or large `.tscn` dumps.
- Insufficient context → **stop and ask**. Never invent UX, paths, or game feel.
- Shortest complete answer. No restating the task, no pasted diffs (the PR is the diff).
- If the chat drifts beyond the ticket, say so and stop.
- Two failed attempts: stop, note under Outcome, ask.

## Models
| Work | Model | Effort |
|---|---|---|
| `/refine` | Auto | Medium |
| `/implement`, `/address`, `/done` | Auto | Low |
| Hard bug (new chat + diagnosing-bugs) | Auto | Medium |
| Avoid for routine tickets | High effort | |

